{"title":"2014 UK MOG Problems/Problem 5a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UK_MOG_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 UK MOG Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UK_MOG_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The AM-GM inequality states that, for positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9fda793b76a6b511c55605873948d6d30cc16ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1}, x_{2}, \\cdots, x_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b17dce7bb11bff2a5e23ee066d6030863150e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_{1} + x_{2} + \\cdots + x_{n}}{n} \\geq \\sqrt[n]{x_{1}x_{2}\\cdots x_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"273\" height=\"37\" /></center>\n<p>Moreover, equality holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/5905cda7220e89c0aa16b89312c37ed34efdf85d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1} = x_{2} = \\cdots = x_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UK_MOG_Problems/Problem_5a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/89504edc4b9768a0e09ff21ff0986d2c2f037251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{c}{a} \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" /></center>\n<p>for all positive real numbers a, b and c, and determine when equality holds.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_UK_MOG_Problems/Problem_5a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the AM-GM inequality and the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a natural number, we can recognise:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8ca4702bbfcc8095260dec2569dcf9363134156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1} + x_{2} + \\cdots + x_{n - 1} + x_{n} \\geq n \\times \\sqrt[n]{x_{1}x_{2} \\cdots x_{n - 1}x_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"397\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We can then use this with the left-hand side by allowing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/1302d35c82f55e038df06903f3be77bf99bbd2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1} = \\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40f0487c8306f49f59ae0b279b59847ee188fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2} = \\frac{b}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cfc16e50fa49c062202882481b80b51250f7df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{3} = \\frac{c}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/074cebd1cc5027d56061d8ff87b694da7236d1a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{c}{a} \\geq 3 \\times \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{a}{b} \\times \\frac{b}{c} \\times \\frac{c}{a}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"243\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59442aba6792cf63aaaa3bd5ac07363f629fa4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{c}{a} \\geq 3 \\times \\sqrt[3]{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Therefore:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/89504edc4b9768a0e09ff21ff0986d2c2f037251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{c}{a} \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" /><br />\nwith equality holding when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047038efe86590c33542af72d036aeb44bcd1154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{c}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"39\" />, which happens only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec0ce3f851e9d124ca3388a8bbdebb383a00f9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are all real.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018150247\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.691 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 66/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3639/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.305      1 2014_UK_MOG_Problems/Problem_5\n100.00%    7.305      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:38074:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018150247 and revision id 293990. Rendering was triggered because: page-edit\n -->\n</div>"}